<Base lang="en" title="Hiring process — TailorMind">
  <h1>Hiring process</h1>
  <p>Four stages, about two weeks. Everything async until the interview, and two live conversations at the end.</p>

  <h2>Stage 1 — Application review <small>(~5 days)</small></h2>
  <p>You apply from your terminal: clone the challenge repo, open your agent and type <code>/tm-apply</code>. It asks for your CV, LinkedIn and <strong>the specification you would start the challenge with</strong>, and hands you your key. The <a href={`${b}/en/apply/`}>form</a> is there too and costs you nothing — but the job is directing agents, so which door you come through says something.</p>
  <p>We screen for fit and, above all, read what you wrote.</p>

  <h2>Stage 2 — Take-home <small>(required · 30 minutes, 40 with the extension)</small></h2>
  <p><strong>It is required: no submitted take-home, no Stage 3.</strong> How it works is <a href={`${b}/en/take-home/`}>explained here</a>: a platformer in Lua with LÖVE, 30 minutes (40 if they take the minute-30 extension), and the requirements arriving while they work — more of them than fit. The task itself downloads when the run opens; it is not published. Same three scores as the interview — Criterio, Autonomy, Tech.</p>

  <h2>Stage 3 — Technical interview <small>(40 min, live)</small></h2>
  <p>One live conversation, three parts:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Culture &amp; background.</strong> CV walk-through, recent projects, how you work, mutual fit.</li>
    <li><strong>Take-home review.</strong> Discuss your submission — decisions, trade-offs, what you'd change. We probe for <em>resulting</em> and hindsight bias on a recent decision you bring (what / why / expected / confidence %).</li>
    <li><strong>Technical problem.</strong> A small live problem or an extension of the take-home, pair-coding with Claude.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><small><strong>Decision window:</strong> we email you with an outcome — offer or polite reject — within ~5 business days of the interview. We will not leave you hanging; if we need more time we say so.</small></p>

  <h2>Stage 4 — Final interview and offer</h2>
  <p>If we move forward, we send the offer in writing and follow up with a 30–45 min call to walk through compensation, contract type, and start date.</p>

  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Criterio</strong> — judgment under uncertainty (Kahneman/Klein, Tetlock, Duke).</li>
    <li><strong>Autonomy</strong> — drives ambiguous work to clarity without micromanagement.</li>
    <li><strong>AI fluency</strong> — uses Claude as a force multiplier, not a crutch.</li>
    <li><strong>Engineering rigor</strong> — full-stack quality, tests, docs.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
